---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
import Notice from '../components/Notice.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Legal Information — AiLawyer.world"
  description="Legal information, research boundaries, and disclaimers for AiLawyer.world."
  canonical="https://ailawyer.world/legal/"
  theme="paper"
  accent="legal"
  eyebrow="LEGAL INFORMATION"
  heading="Legal Information"
  lead="AiLawyer.world is an experimental legal-AI research and information project developed within EN-DO Technology."
  width="article"
>
  <div slot="pre-heading" class="status-row">
    <Badge>SERVICE BOUNDARY: ACTIVE</Badge>
  </div>

  <div class="legal-notice">
    <Notice tone="warning">
      The content published on this website is provided for general
      informational and research purposes only. It is not legal advice.
    </Notice>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>No attorney-client relationship</h2>

    <p>
      Using this website, reading its publications, or interacting with any
      future experimental system does not create an attorney-client
      relationship or any other professional relationship.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No legal representation</h2>

    <p>AiLawyer.world does not:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>represent users before courts, agencies, or other authorities;</li>
      <li>file lawsuits, applications, appeals, or other documents;</li>
      <li>guarantee legal outcomes;</li>
      <li>replace advice from a qualified lawyer;</li>
      <li>provide emergency, medical, or psychological services.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Jurisdiction and legal changes</h2>

    <p>
      Laws and procedures vary by jurisdiction and may change over time.
      General information may not apply to a particular country, state,
      city, court, agency, date, or individual situation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sources and uncertainty</h2>

    <p>
      AiLawyer.world researches architectures that connect legal statements
      with identifiable sources and explicit verification states. However,
      no experimental system should be treated as complete, infallible, or
      suitable for every legal matter.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Professional assistance</h2>

    <p>
      Users facing deadlines, court proceedings, financial consequences,
      immigration matters, criminal allegations, safety concerns, or other
      serious risks should consult an appropriately qualified professional.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Research status</h2>

    <p>
      NEXUS TwinLoop Legal Lab, Code AVIN, REG-containers, and related
      architectures are research concepts or laboratory prototypes unless
      expressly identified otherwise.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    /*
     * Legal Information belongs to the
     * Paper / Legal family.
     * All colors come from Design System tokens.
     */

    .status-row {
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-notice {
      --accent-secondary: var(--paper-orange);
      --page-muted: var(--paper-orange-text);
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    section {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--page-border);
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      color: var(--page-text);
      font-size: 1.6rem;
    }

    p {
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    ul {
      padding-left: 1.4rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    li + li {
      margin-top: 0.55rem;
    }

  </style>
</PageLayout>